Report a source directory that cp -R cannot open.
When opendir() failed on a source directory, as for one without read
permission, or on Windows one whose path is too long to list,
copy_file() had already created the destination directory and returned
failure without a message. cp -R then left an empty directory and
exited with status 1 without saying why. Use warn_opendir() so that
the failure is reported like the others.

---
 libbb/copy_file.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/libbb/copy_file.c
+++ b/libbb/copy_file.c
@@ -202,7 +202,7 @@
 		add_to_ino_dev_hashtable(&dest_stat, NULL);
 
 		/* Recursively copy files in SOURCE */
-		dp = opendir(source);
+		dp = warn_opendir(source);
 		if (dp == NULL) {
 			retval = -1;
 			goto preserve_mode_ugid_time;
